  <simpara>
    The documentation toolchain consists of bundled tools, which are checked into the repository under <filename>documentation/tools/</filename>, and runtime dependencies, which must be installed separately.
  </simpara>
  <section>
    <title>Bundled tools</title>
    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Saxon HE 12.7</term>
        <listitem>
          <simpara>
            XSLT processor used to run transformations.
            Located at <filename>documentation/tools/saxon/</filename>.
          </simpara>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Jing</term>
        <listitem>
          <simpara>
            RELAX NG validator.
            Located at <filename>documentation/tools/jing/</filename>.
          </simpara>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>SchXslt2 1.11.1</term>
        <listitem>
          <simpara>
            Compiles Schematron schemas into XSLT validation stylesheets, run with Saxon.
            Located at <filename>documentation/tools/schematron/schxslt2/</filename>.
          </simpara>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </section>
  <section>
    <title>Runtime dependencies</title>
    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Java 21 or later</term>
        <listitem>
          <simpara>
            Required to run Saxon and Jing.
            Install OpenJDK 21 via your system package manager (for example, <package>default-jdk</package> on Debian-based systems).
          </simpara>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>xmllint</term>
        <listitem>
          <simpara>
            Required for XSD validation.
            Available as part of the <package>libxml2-utils</package> package on Debian-based systems.
          </simpara>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </section>
</chapter>
